  "style": [
    "Register: chronicle/log lines (log.*, battle.log.*, battle.summary.*, prisoner.*, duel.round.*) and narration in bios/events/city & sect descriptions use plain である/past-tense narration (「{officer}が{city}の商業を{value}まで発展させた（+{amount}）。」). No です/ます in narration.",
    "System messages, hints, reasons and confirmations (ui.*, order.reason.*, army.reason.*, trade/donate/reward.reason.*, error.*) use concise polite です・ます (「都市を選択してください。」「金が足りません（必要{cost}、{city}に{gold}）。」). UI labels/buttons/tabs are noun phrases without verbs or polite endings, ideally <= 8 kanji/kana; short stat names are 2 characters (武力/統率/知力/政治/魅力).",
    "Character speech: advisors address the player as 殿 with archaic polite speech (〜にございます／〜でございましょう); the Azure Court addresses Liu Chengxuan as 殿下, the Southern Lotus addresses Su Wanqing as 陛下, the Wolf Riders say 大可汗, Black Mountain outlaws say 兄者 in rough but dignified speech. The tavern innkeeper speaks plain, slightly rustic polite speech. Rumors (rumor.*, officer.*.rumor) are tavern hearsay ending in 〜という噂だ／〜らしい／〜とか.",
    "Event choices (event.*.choice.N) are short decisions in plain form (「兵を送って討伐する」「金を払って立ち去らせる（金300）」); costs go in full-width parentheses as （金300） / （兵糧3000）. event.*.effect.N and event.choice.ok are narration (「やむを得まい。」 for 'So be it.').",
    "Names: officers, cities, factions, sects and techniques are written in kanji only (shinjitai forms of the scenario nameZh), no furigana, no katakana, no space or middle dot inside a name (慕容嘯, 赫連勃, 東方策). 龍 is kept in names (龍鉄樹) as in Koei titles; 琅琊 is written 琅邪 as in Koei's Japanese releases. Banner glyphs are single kanji (燕 赫 劉 沈 蘇 墨).",
    "Epithets: use the glossary epithet; with the name show it as 「{epithet}」{name} (suggested ui.strategy.nameWithEpithet = 「{epithet}」{name}). When an epithet is quoted in prose (e.g. 'the Quick Knife'), reuse the same Japanese epithet in 「」.",
    "Factions: drop the English article ('the {faction}' -> {faction}). Faction names already end in 軍/騎/盟/寨, so never append 軍 to {faction} (use {faction}の部隊, {faction}の兵). 'the Brotherhood' in prose = 黒山寨 (or 山寨 when repeated), 'the League' = 東海盟. 'Nine Provinces' = 九洲 (never 九州, which reads as Kyushu); 'the realm' = 天下.",
    "Numbers and placeholders: keep every {placeholder} name exactly; reorder freely for Japanese word order (SOV). Use counters after numbers: {count}人 (officers), {count}都市, {days}日, {months}か月, {age}歳, {year}年{month}月. Quantities read 金{gold}, 兵糧{food}, 兵力{troops} in labels; in prose '{troops} troops' -> {troops}の兵. Digits, %, +, -, / stay half-width (成功率{chance}%, 士気+{amount}).",
    "Punctuation: Japanese full-width punctuation in Japanese text: 、。！？：（）「」 (nested quotes 『』); English double-spaces used as column gaps become a full-width space (「金 {gold}　兵糧 {food}」); trailing '...' on buttons becomes … (「登用…」). Keep the sort markers '^'/'v' and other format characters as they are.",
    "Terminology follows Koei Japanese releases: 武将, 君主, 太守, 勢力, 在野, 兵力, 兵糧, 金, 治安, 農業, 商業, 防御/城壁, 訓練, 士気, 忠誠, 登用, 探索, 褒美, 出陣, 計略 (火計/混乱/鼓舞), 一騎討ち. The monthly planning phase is 評定; the execution phase is 進行. The army leader is 主将 and the others 副将; an army is named after its leader ({commander}隊).",
    "Wuxia terms: sect = 門派 (Martial Sects = 武林門派), sect leader = 掌門, Moonwell Hall's mistress = 堂主, Stone Bell's abbot = 方丈, martial technique = 武技 ('mastered the technique {technique}' -> 「{technique}」を会得した), duel rounds counted in 合 ({round}/{max}合), duel moves 強撃/虚撃/防御 (強撃 beats 虚撃, 虚撃 beats 防御, 防御 beats 強撃), duel HP = 体力.",
    "Allusions: the Yin Hexuan event mirrors 三顧の礼 (title may read 「霧深き山への三顧」); the Jade Seal is 伝国の玉璽; Situ Kang's epithet 敗軍の将 alludes to 「敗軍の将は兵を語らず」. Chancellor (title) = 丞相, Wen Tingjian's epithet 'the Grand Chancellor' = 相国."
  ],
